# Copy this file to `.env` beside it, at the repo root, and fill it in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env          (PowerShell: copy .env.example .env)
#
# The repo-root .env is the solution-level config for the whole stack. It is what
# docker-compose.yml loads for the api, worker and beat services (`env_file: .env`), and
# what app/config.py picks up first for host-side runs. A backend/.env is still read as a
# fallback if no root .env exists; if both exist the root one wins.
#
# The process environment always overrides the file. Every setting not listed here has a
# default in app/config.py — only the AI provider block below is required to boot.

# ===========================================================================
# AI provider — pick ONE block
# ===========================================================================
# Startup requires at least one of OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or LLM_BASE_URL.
# The deterministic half of the pipeline (collectors, signals, decision engine,
# rule-based reports, report recompute) runs with no model configured at all.

# --- Local OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp, TGI) ---
# Three things that cost time if you get them wrong:
#   1. The /v1 suffix is required. LLM_BASE_URL is passed verbatim to ChatOpenAI.
#   2. LLM_API_KEY must be non-empty even though local servers ignore it — the OpenAI
#      client rejects an empty key.
#   3. The served model MUST support tool calling. The analyst is tool-driven: it reads
#      the evidence bundle off a virtual filesystem with ls/read_file/glob/grep.
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# LLM_MODEL=qwen3:32b
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1   # Ollama :11434 | vLLM :8000 | LM Studio :1234
# LLM_API_KEY=not-needed
# LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.0
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=                      # optional; blank disables failover
#
# 4. Running under docker compose, "localhost" is the *container*, not your machine. A
#    model server on the host is reached at host.docker.internal instead — compose already
#    maps it (extra_hosts: host.docker.internal:host-gateway) for api and worker:
#      LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#    The analyst runs in the `worker` container, so that is the one that must reach it.

# --- Hosted OpenAI (the default; behaves exactly as it did pre-LangGraph) ---
LLM_PROVIDER=openai
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as well and the analyst fails over to it automatically.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# --- Hosted Anthropic ---
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Analyst limits (apply to every provider).
# ANALYST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS bounds the whole agent run, not one HTTP request — an agent
# loop makes several.
# ANALYST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180
# ANALYST_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=16000

# ===========================================================================
# Infrastructure
# ===========================================================================
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://threatintel:threatintel@localhost:5432/threatintel
DATABASE_SYNC_URL=postgresql://threatintel:threatintel@localhost:5432/threatintel
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/1

# ===========================================================================
# Collector / enrichment API keys — all optional; a missing key is reported as a
# data gap rather than failing the investigation.
# ===========================================================================
VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY=
ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY=
URLSCAN_API_KEY=
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
ANYRUN_API_KEY=
OTX_API_KEY=
SHODAN_API_KEY=
PHISHTANK_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_SAFE_BROWSING_API_KEY=
OPENCTI_API_URL=
OPENCTI_API_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# App
# ===========================================================================
APP_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
